{
  "id": "motion-aftereffect",
  "term": "motion aftereffect",
  "definition": "A motion aftereffect is a change in motion perception that occurs after viewing a motion signal, shifting later judgments about movement direction. In this source, it refers to a bias produced even by static images that imply motion, such as another person’s gaze toward an object.",
